# Syllabus Planner — Project Stack

Monorepo layout:

- `frontend/` — TypeScript + Next.js (App Router)
- `backend/` — Python FastAPI + SQLModel
- `docker-compose.yml` — dev stack (Postgres, backend, frontend with live reload)
- `docker-compose.prod.yml` — production stack

## Package managers (mandatory)

| Area             | Tool     | Never use           |
| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------- |
| Node / frontend  | **pnpm** | npm, yarn, bun      |
| Python / backend | **uv**   | pip, poetry, pipenv |

```bash
# Frontend
cd frontend && pnpm install

# Frontend test
cd frontend && pnpm test

# Backend
cd backend && uv sync --extra dev
```

## Docker-first development

Prefer Docker Compose for dev, test, and production-like runs:

```bash
# Day-to-day dev (live reload — no rebuild on code edits)
docker compose --profile local-db up --build

# Production-like image (code baked in; rebuild to pick up changes)
docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up --build
```

When running commands locally, use the same tools as Dockerfiles (`pnpm`, `uv`).

## Agents-first API

Every user-facing action must exist in the FastAPI backend first. Add or update `.cursor/skills/syllabus-planner-api.skill.md` before building frontend features that depend on new endpoints.
